  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given two increasing arrays of NNN integers x1&lt;x2&lt;…&lt;xNx_1 \\lt x_2 \\lt \\ldots \\lt x_Nx1​&lt;x2​&lt;…&lt;xN​ and y1&lt;y2&lt;…&lt;yNy_1 \\lt y_2 \\lt \\ldots \\lt y_Ny1​&lt;y2​&lt;…&lt;yN​.\n\nFor a permutation σ1,σ2,…,σN\\sigma_1,\\sigma_2,\\ldots,\\sigma_Nσ1​,σ2​,…,σN​ of integers 1,2,…,N1,2,\\ldots,N1,2,…,N, let's define A(σ)A(\\sigma)A(σ) in the following way:\n\n\nConsider the points (x1,yσ1),(x2,yσ2),…,(xN,yσN)(x_1, y_{\\sigma_1}), (x_2, y_{\\sigma_2}), \\ldots, (x_N, y_{\\sigma_N})(x1​,yσ1​​),(x2​,yσ2​​),…,(xN​,yσN​​). Then A(σ)A(\\sigma)A(σ) equals to the area of the convex hull of these points.\nLet SSS be the sum of A(σ)A(\\sigma)A(σ) over all n!n!n! permutations. One can show that 2S2S2S is an integer under the constraints of the problem.\n\nFind the remainder of 2S2S2S modulo 998 244 353998\\,244\\,353998244353.\n\n\nInput Format\n\n\nThe first line contains a single integer TTT, the number of test cases. The description of test cases follows.\n\n\n\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN −-− the length of the two arrays.\n\n\n\n\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN integers x1,x2,…,xNx_1, x_2,\\dots, x_Nx1​,x2​,…,xN​ (x1&lt;x2&lt;…&lt;xNx_1 \\lt x_2 \\lt \\ldots \\lt x_Nx1​&lt;x2​&lt;…&lt;xN​).\n\n\n\n\nThe third line of each test case contains NNN integers y1,y2,…,yNy_1, y_2,\\dots, y_Ny1​,y2​,…,yN​ (y1&lt;y2&lt;…&lt;yNy_1 \\lt y_2 \\lt \\ldots \\lt y_Ny1​&lt;y2​&lt;…&lt;yN​).\n\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case print the remainder of 2S2S2S modulo 998 244 353998\\,244\\,353998244353.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤101 \\le T \\le 101≤T≤10",
      "3≤N≤303 \\le N \\le 303≤N≤30",
      "−1000≤xi≤1000-1000 \\le x_i \\le 1000−1000≤xi​≤1000",
      "−1000≤yi≤1000-1000 \\le y_i \\le 1000−1000≤yi​≤1000",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases doesn't exceed 303030"
