        "explanation": "Explanation:\nHere are the weights of all permutations from the first test case:\n\n\nFor σ=(1,2,3)\\sigma = (1, 2, 3)σ=(1,2,3), we have points (1,1),(2,2),(3,3)(1, 1), (2, 2), (3, 3)(1,1),(2,2),(3,3). They are collinear, so area of their convex hull is 000: A(σ)=0A(\\sigma) = 0A(σ)=0.\n\n\nFor σ=(1,3,2)\\sigma = (1, 3, 2)σ=(1,3,2), we have points (1,1),(2,3),(3,2)(1, 1), (2, 3), (3, 2)(1,1),(2,3),(3,2). Their convex hull is the triangle with vertices in them, and its area is 32\\frac{3}{2}23​: A(σ)=32A(\\sigma) = \\frac{3}{2}A(σ)=23​.\n\n\nFor σ=(2,1,3)\\sigma = (2, 1, 3)σ=(2,1,3), we have points (1,2),(2,1),(3,3)(1, 2), (2, 1), (3, 3)(1,2),(2,1),(3,3). Their convex hull is the triangle with vertices in them, and its area is 32\\frac{3}{2}23​: A(σ)=32A(\\sigma) = \\frac{3}{2}A(σ)=23​.\n\n\nFor σ=(2,3,1)\\sigma = (2, 3, 1)σ=(2,3,1), we have points (1,2),(2,3),(3,1)(1, 2), (2, 3), (3, 1)(1,2),(2,3),(3,1). Their convex hull is the triangle with vertices in them, and its area is 32\\frac{3}{2}23​: A(σ)=32A(\\sigma) = \\frac{3}{2}A(σ)=23​.\n\n\nFor σ=(3,1,2)\\sigma = (3, 1, 2)σ=(3,1,2), we have points (1,3),(2,1),(3,2)(1, 3), (2, 1), (3, 2)(1,3),(2,1),(3,2). Their convex hull is the triangle with vertices in them, and its area is 32\\frac{3}{2}23​: A(σ)=32A(\\sigma) = \\frac{3}{2}A(σ)=23​.\n\n\nFor σ=(3,2,1)\\sigma = (3, 2, 1)σ=(3,2,1), we have points (1,3),(2,2),(3,1)(1, 3), (2, 2), (3, 1)(1,3),(2,2),(3,1). They are collinear, so area of their convex hull is 000: A(σ)=0A(\\sigma) = 0A(σ)=0.\n\n\nSum of these values is 666, so the answer to this test case is 2⋅6=122\\cdot 6 = 122⋅6=12."
      }
